msgid "The default board is 8 by 8, with 12 pieces on each side. A 10 by 10 board gives each player 20 pieces; a 12 by 12 board gives 30. The two middle rows start empty. Size changes the space and starting army, not the selected movement rules."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/monopoly.rb:41
msgid "The default board is American / Atlantic City. A different board can change names, layout, currency, starting cash, Start salary and property economics. Larger boards also have more colour groups, stations and utilities. The profiles below are generated from the boards actually used by Game Room. Inspect individual deeds for purchase prices, rent levels and mortgage values."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/monopoly.rb:41
msgid "The default board is American / Atlantic City. A different board can change names, layout, currency, starting cash, Start salary and property economics. Larger boards also have more colour groups, stations and utilities. The profiles below are generated from the boards actually used by Power Games. Inspect individual deeds for purchase prices, rent levels and mortgage values."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/bridge.rb:11
msgid "The default game is a rubber. It ends when a pair has won two games, and the pair with more points overall wins the match. The scoring chapters explain how individual deals build towards that result."
msgstr "Ve výchozím nastavení hrajete robra. Končí, když jedna dvojice vyhraje dvě hry. O vítězi celého zápasu rozhoduje součet bodů, nikoli samotný počet vyhraných her."

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:242
msgid "The default is four players and East and South rounds, with 30,000 starting points each. Everyone completes a dealer period in East, then in South: at least eight hands, with dealer continuations adding more. Payments and accepted Riichi deposits change the balances during the match."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:437
msgid "The default match has four wind rounds and exactly sixteen hands, with balances starting at zero. East, South, West and North each last four hands. The dealer always changes after a hand, so a dealer win or a draw does not add an extra repeat."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:122
msgid "The default match has four wind rounds: East, South, West and North. Every player completes a dealer period in each round, making at least sixteen hands. Hand payments accumulate from zero; winning one hand does not necessarily win the match."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default settings are the classic rules. The table creator may change entry, extra-roll, exact-finish, three-sixes and blockade rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default values are 1000 points to win, 30 points to bank a turn and 50 points for the first bank."
msgstr ""

msgid "The default variant deals two private cards to each player. There are four betting rounds: before the flop, after the three-card flop, after the one-card turn, and after the one-card river. The five table cards are shared. At showdown choose the best five cards from the seven available: both, one or neither of your private cards may be used. The game announces each stage and newly exposed table cards."
