msgid "When a banked total reaches the score limit, finish the current circuit through the last player in seating order. Players who already played in this circuit do not get an extra turn. The highest final score wins; equal highest scores end in a draw. Saved games from before version 2.0 retain the immediate-win rule."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/battleship.rb:13
msgid "When a new game starts, each player chooses Randomly or Manually. Randomly places and seals your whole fleet at once, using the selected fleet and the rule about ships touching. Choose Manually if you want to decide where each ship goes: only then does the placement board open. Your choice does not affect how your opponent arranges their fleet."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/monopoly.rb:16
msgid "When a purchase becomes an auction"
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:482
msgid "When adding questions to an existing set, choose the language first, then press Enter to choose a set in a separate window. Set names no longer repeat the language code. Delete removes a selected draft after confirmation. The main-menu entry is now called Create your own quiz question sets."
msgstr "Při přidávání otázek do existující sady nejprve vyberete jazyk a potvrdíte Enterem. Sadu pak vyberete v samostatném okně. Názvy sad už neopakují kód jazyka. Delete po potvrzení odstraní vybraný koncept. Položka v hlavní nabídce se nyní jmenuje Tvorba vlastních sad kvízových otázek."

#: games/generated/rulebooks/categories.rb:13
msgid "When all sheets are submitted or the answer time ends, writing closes and the answers are revealed. The judge sees identical answers grouped within each category and decides whether they fit the letter, category and meaning. This is not automatic dictionary scoring: discuss doubtful entries with the judge."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:167 games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:286 games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:71
msgid "When another player discards, the response list offers only legal choices. Select Pass if you do not want the tile. To claim it, choose Chow, Pung, Kong or Declare Mahjong and press Enter. A chow may be claimed only from the player immediately before you. A pung or kong can use a discard from any opponent."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:209
msgid "When assigning teams, Shift+Up and Shift+Down swap the selected person or bot with their neighbour. The cursor follows that person, and movement stops at the ends of the list."
msgstr "Při přiřazování týmů prohodí Shift+šipka nahoru a Shift+šipka dolů vybranou osobu nebo bota se sousedem v seznamu. Kurzor zůstane na přesouvané osobě a na začátku i konci seznamu se přesouvání zastaví."

#: games/generated/rulebooks/poker.rb:34
msgid "When blinds are used, you can leave them unchanged, increase them after a chosen number of hands, or increase them after a number of minutes. The default doubles them every five hands. The interval accepts 1–100 hands or minutes and the multiplier 2–10. A change takes effect only at the start of a new hand, never halfway through a bet."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/battleship.rb:19
msgid "When both fleets are ready, the first player at the table begins. On your turn, choose a square in Enemy waters and press Enter. A miss means there is no ship there. A hit means you struck part of a ship. Hit and sunk means every square of that particular ship has now been hit."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:434
msgid "When creating a table, the default language of questions, words or cards now follows the Power Games interface language. If that language is unavailable, English is selected. Your saved settings still take precedence."
msgstr "Při vytváření stolu se výchozí jazyk otázek, slov nebo karet nyní řídí jazykem rozhraní Power Games. Pokud příslušný jazyk není k dispozici, vybere se angličtina. Vaše uložená nastavení mají i nadále přednost."

#: games/generated/rulebooks/quiz.rb:16
msgid "When creating or configuring the table, first choose a question language and then a set offered in that language. The set label gives the number of questions supplied. This choice does not change anyone's interface: a Polish interface can still display questions from an English or Italian set. The language and set are shared by the whole table."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/axel_pong.rb:17
msgid "When creating the table, choose 7, 11 or 21 points to win, or select Custom number. With Custom number selected, Tab takes you to an edit field where you can enter a whole number from 2 to 999. In both Single and Doubles, reaching the target is not enough: you also need a lead of at least two points. At 10–10 in an 11-point match, 11–10 does not end the match; 12–10 does. The last choice, Unlimited, keeps counting points without declaring a winner or ending the match because of the score. Play continues until the table is closed or its owner ends the match with Ctrl+Q."
msgstr ""

msgid "When enabled, eight buzzer cards are added to the classic or No Mercy deck. A buzzer can be played on anything and anything can be played on it. After it is played, every active player presses B; the last player draws two cards."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/scopa.rb:16
msgid "When everyone has played their hand, more cards are dealt. Once the deck and all hands are empty, the last player to have made a capture receives the cards left on the table. The round is then scored, and the next player becomes dealer."
msgstr ""

msgid "When it is time to roll, press Enter anywhere on the board. After the roll, choose a pawn and press Enter, then choose its marked destination and press Enter. Press P for your pawn fields, Shift+P for the opponents' pawn fields, T for the turn and Ctrl+F1 for these rules."
msgstr "Když je čas házet, stiskněte Enter kdekoli na hrací desce. Po hodu vyberte figurku a stiskněte Enter, poté vyberte její označené cílové pole a stiskněte Enter. Klávesou P přečtete pole svých figurek, Shift+P pole figurek soupeřů, T zjistíte, kdo je na tahu, a Ctrl+F1 otevřete tato pravidla."

msgid "When no tile can be played, draw one with Space. If a legal move remains, play it; otherwise your train opens and the turn passes automatically. With an empty boneyard, no legal move opens your train and automatically passes without drawing. Other players may then use that train until you play on it."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/makao.rb:27
msgid "When one card remains, announce Makao. Another player may catch an omission before your next turn and make you draw the configured penalty. You can announce or catch Makao during someone else's turn, including a bot's delay. Playing your last card wins immediately; this game does not run a points-elimination tournament."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:48
msgid "When one player wins, each loser pays that winner the amount due. A tie for first place means no one pays anyone, even if other players scored less. You can never lose more feathers than you have. Separate penalties for exceeding 21 or 25 still apply."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:346
msgid "When opening Game Room, you can download and install a newer version available in ELTEN. Updating is optional: choosing No keeps the installed version, and an update never interrupts an open game. After updating, Game Room returns to the requested table or invitation."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/audio_ball.rb:26
msgid "When playing a bot, difficulty also affects its reaction time and mistakes: higher levels mean faster reactions and fewer wrong defences. The bot follows the same rules for preparing, hitting and defending the ball as a person."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/axel_pong.rb:40
msgid "When playing another person, Ctrl+W warns the opponent to serve within ten seconds. It is available only after the normal break, while it is their serve and the ball has not been served yet. A valid serve cancels the warning; otherwise you receive a point. Repeated presses do not extend the deadline, and a new warning cannot be sent for fifteen seconds. Observers cannot issue warnings. A broken connection does not count as a late serve."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:28
msgid "When several identical tiles are available, consider which copies to remove. Removing an edge tile may free its neighbour; removing an upper tile uncovers one below. Not every available pair leads to a solution. Undo the last pair lets you return and try another order."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/axel_pong.rb:41
msgid "When the connection is interrupted"
msgstr ""

msgid "When the draw pile is exhausted, discards are shuffled for drawing again; players keep their current hands. Reaching a round-ending total starts a fresh deal for the remaining players, resetting the pile total, not their token balances."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/battleship.rb:24
msgid "When the last ship sinks, both programs reveal their fleets for a final check. The game verifies the original placement and every answer. Only then is the result final. A fleet or answer that disagrees with the original sealed placement makes that player lose; if both fail the check, the result is a draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mancala.rb:24
msgid "When the opposing row is empty, you must feed it if a legal move can do so. If the player whose turn comes next has no legal move, all seeds still on the board go to the person who made the last move. This also applies when the next player has seeds but cannot feed the empty opposing row. Game Room uses this particular Ayoayo variant; other published descriptions may award these seeds differently."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mancala.rb:24
msgid "When the opposing row is empty, you must feed it if a legal move can do so. If the player whose turn comes next has no legal move, all seeds still on the board go to the person who made the last move. This also applies when the next player has seeds but cannot feed the empty opposing row. Power Games uses this particular Ayoayo variant; other published descriptions may award these seeds differently."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/farkle.rb:18
msgid "When the same selected dice have more than one scoring interpretation, you receive the highest valid value. These are Game Room's values; changing the winning score or banking minimum does not change this scoring table."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/farkle.rb:18
msgid "When the same selected dice have more than one scoring interpretation, you receive the highest valid value. These are Power Games's values; changing the winning score or banking minimum does not change this scoring table."
msgstr ""

msgid "When the stock empties, all discards except the top one are shuffled into it. If drawing is impossible, you may continue with the other legal actions. After two complete circuits without drawing or placing a card from the original hand, while no draw source remains, the round is blocked. Merely taking and replacing table cards does not count as progress."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/poker.rb:24
msgid "When the types match, compare the ranks forming the combination, then the remaining cards, called kickers. Suits never break a tie. An ace is normally high, but A-2-3-4-5 is the lowest straight. G says No combination when you only have a high card; that does not mean your cards are ignored at showdown. Equal best five-card hands split the pot."
msgstr ""

msgid "When time expires, everything currently entered is submitted automatically. The fields are not cleared before the server accepts the answers."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/makao.rb:28 games/generated/rulebooks/mexican_train.rb:23
msgid "When time runs out"
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:251
msgid "When watching Axel Pong, C reads the selected player's name and paddle position. Victory and defeat are also heard from that player's or team's perspective at the end of the match."
msgstr ""

msgid "When you are allowed to see the card, arrows browse it, C reads it all, 1 reads the target and 2–6 the forbidden words. R reads remaining time, S team scores and T the describer and team. Guessers and observers have no active-card reading shortcuts."
msgstr "Pokud smíte vidět kartu, šipkami ji procházíte, C ji přečte celou, 1 přečte hledané slovo a 2–6 zakázaná slova. R přečte zbývající čas, S skóre týmů a T popisujícího hráče a tým. Hádající hráči a pozorovatelé nemají zkratky pro čtení aktivní karty."

#: games/generated/rulebooks/farkle.rb:19
msgid "When you can stop, and when the game ends"
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:515
msgid "When you enter an invalid number in an action dialog, the dialog stays open, explains the problem and selects the value so you can correct it immediately."
msgstr "Pokud v dialogu akce zadáte nepovolené číslo, okno zůstane otevřené, vysvětlí chybu a označí hodnotu, abyste ji mohli hned opravit."

msgid "When you have no legal starting card, draw one. If it is playable and playing a drawn card is enabled, you can use it immediately, also as part of a packet, or end your turn. Otherwise the turn ends automatically. You cannot draw voluntarily when you already have a legal card. If the drawing pile runs out, discards other than the top card are recycled."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/makao.rb:13
msgid "When you have no legal starting card, draw one. The three ready-made profiles also allow you to draw voluntarily instead of playing a card you already have. Custom rules has an Allow drawing with a playable card checkbox, enabled by default, which you can turn off. If the drawn card is playable and playing a drawn card is enabled, you may play it immediately, also as part of a packet, or press Space again to end your turn without drawing another card. Otherwise the turn ends automatically, even if another card in your hand could be played. This choice does not cancel a drawing or waiting penalty. If the drawing pile runs out, discards other than the top card are recycled."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:115
msgid "When you hold the ball, press A or Right arrow to prepare, then press a shot key to send it. Do the same before serving. Each new incoming ball needs a new defence press after the opponent hits."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:22
msgid "When you land, the square acts first, then its card, then an encounter with another duck. If the square or card moves you again, continue resolving events at the new square."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/quiz.rb:23
msgid "When you leave the table, you will be asked whether you want to report the marked questions. Choose Yes, describe the problem with each question and press Send. The question and its answers are included automatically. Choosing No discards the marks; they are not saved for later."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/monopoly.rb:31
msgid "When you owe more cash than you have"
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/yahtzee.rb:12
msgid "When you stop rolling, choose a category from the scoring list. The list tells you how many points the current dice would give there. A category whose requirement you did not meet is usually worth zero, but you may still sacrifice it to save a more useful row for later."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/duck_racing.rb:42
msgid "When you thaw, you receive five feathers. If another effect gave you feathers while frozen, you keep those too. Freezing and other missed turns count down together, rather than one after the other."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/mahjong.rb:41
msgid "When your drawn tile completes a legal winning hand, use Declare Mahjong instead of discarding. To win on another player’s discard, select the winning response. Seven pairs and thirteen orphans are alternative winning shapes where the selected scoring profile permits them. Completing a shape alone is not enough if the variant requires a minimum score or yaku."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/scientific_war.rb:15
msgid "When your hand is empty after a trick, you pick up your pile and it becomes your new hand. If your pile is empty too, you are out of the game."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/tysiac.rb:33
msgid "When your score reaches the interval from 120 below the target to just below the target, it is set to exactly 120 below and you go onto the barrel. At the usual target this means 880. Defender points no longer increase your score there. You have three deals to win and fulfil a contract of at least 120."
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/ninety_nine.rb:21
msgid "When your time runs out"
msgstr ""

#: games/generated/rulebooks/yahtzee.rb:21
msgid "Whenever you roll five equal dice, you may score them in any unused category, even if you previously entered zero in Yahtzee. The roll uses these special scores:"
msgstr "Pět stejných kostek můžeš zapsat do kterékoli volné kategorie, i když už máš v Yahtzee nulu. Pro takový hod platí zvláštní bodování:"

